IMPORT prelude

-- Corporations Act 2001 (Cth) -- the dates the claimant's questions count, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library, and defines no YMD. The Act counts in plain days ("within 28 days after being given
-- notice", s 1056(2); "within 28 days after being so notified", s 1056A(1); "not later than the 28th day after the day on
-- which a copy of the determination ... is given", s 1057(2)(a); "at least 90 days have passed since the previous
-- disclosure", s 1317AAD(1)(b); "the period of 14 days starting on", s 1019B(3)), in business days ("the end of the
-- fifth business day after the day on which the product was issued", s 1019B(3)(b); s 9 "business day means a day that
-- is not a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday or bank holiday in the place concerned") and in years ("within 6 years
-- after the contravention", s 961M(6); "within 6 years after the day on which the cause of action arose", s 1041I(2);
-- "no later than 6 years after the contravention", s 1317K).
--
-- Sourced from the Federal Register of Legislation at 2026-10-13: "Corporations Act 2001", Commonwealth of Australia,
-- licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Corporations Act 2001 claimant's questions`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is on or before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is on or after` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- A number of plain days after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

-- The earlier of two days.
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of` `the first day` `and` `the second day` MEANS
    IF `the first day` `is on or before` `the second day` THEN `the first day` ELSE `the second day`

-- The number of days in a month of a year.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The same day of the month a number of months later; where that month is shorter, its last day (29 February 2028 plus
-- 6 years is 28 February 2034; fork F1 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `months after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the start`) (`the days in month` `the month` `of` `the year`)) `the month` `the year`
    WHERE
        `the months counted` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the start` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the start` MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the year` MEANS FLOOR (`the months counted` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the month` MEANS (`the months counted` MINUS (`the year` TIMES 12)) PLUS 1

-- "Within 6 years after" a day: the period starts the day after and its last day is the same date 6 years on (fork F1).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of 6 years after` `the start` MEANS `the date` 72 `months after` `the start`

-- The day of the week, 0 for Monday to 6 for Sunday, counted from Monday 1 January 1900.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekday number of` `the day` MEANS
    (DATE_SERIAL `the day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1900)) MODULO 7

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `falls on a weekend` IF `the weekday number of` `the day` AT LEAST 5

-- The day reached by counting n weekdays (Monday to Friday) after a day. Public and bank holidays are not known to the
-- encoding; the s 1019B question adds the number of weekday holidays the person counts (fork F9).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the weekday` n `after` `the start` MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN `the start`
    ELSE IF `the next day` `falls on a weekend`
         THEN `the weekday` n `after` `the next day`
         ELSE `the weekday` (n MINUS 1) `after` `the next day`
    WHERE
        `the next day` MEANS `the date` 1 `days after` `the start`
